From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Capossio <capossio.leonardo@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dma: xilinx_axi_dma: keep the error code of a failed
 configure

dma_xilinx_axi_dma_configure() chained the block transfers with
ret = ret || ..., which turns any error into 1. A client that checks
for a negative return, as the Ethernet L2 does on a failed send, took
the failure for success. Return the transfer's own error code.

Signed-off-by: Leonardo Capossio <capossio.leonardo@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/dma/dma_xilinx_axi_dma.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/dma_xilinx_axi_dma.c b/drivers/dma/dma_xilinx_axi_dma.c
index 388df48..47b7bdf 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/dma_xilinx_axi_dma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/dma_xilinx_axi_dma.c
@@ -989,15 +989,14 @@ static int dma_xilinx_axi_dma_configure(const struct device *dev, uint32_t chann
 	LOG_DBG("Completed configuration of AXI DMA - Starting transfer!");
 
 	do {
-		ret = ret ||
-		      dma_xilinx_axi_dma_transfer_block(dev, channel,
+		ret = dma_xilinx_axi_dma_transfer_block(dev, channel,
 							channel == XILINX_AXI_DMA_TX_CHANNEL_NUM
 								? current_block->source_address
 								: current_block->dest_address,
 							current_block->block_size, block_count == 0,
 							current_block->next_block == NULL);
 		block_count++;
-	} while ((current_block = current_block->next_block) && ret == 0);
+	} while (ret == 0 && (current_block = current_block->next_block));
 
 	return ret;
 }
